<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The icons Adwaita has no glyph for: the completion kinds, the drawing tools, the file types
  every file list leads its rows with, a server rack for a remote vault (the theme's
  `network-server` is a box on a cable, or a tower), a breakpoint's dot and ring, a quote
  callout's quotation mark, and a comparison's arrows out of a dashed line that show every
  unchanged line, as GitHub's unfold does. They are shipped with the binary rather than looked up in the
  theme; the prefix is what `IconTheme::add_resource_path` is pointed at, so GTK finds them by
  name like any other icon.
  `filetype-*` rather than `file-*`, which themes already use.
  Every entry is compressed, which GIO undoes on each lookup: their 128 KB take 48 KB in the
  binary (2026-11-05).
-->
<gresources>
